this is inspired by the marantz Cinema 30 stereo receiver VST3 plugin, the Cinema 30's architecture would translate into a high-channel-count virtual channel strip or processing rack in your DAW.

Virtual Signal Chain Architecture

Input & Preamps: A 13.4-channel virtual rack featuring modeled HDAM SA-2 preamps with drive/saturation controls and flexible routing.

DSP & EQ: Built-in 9-band parametric EQ per channel, customizable crossover filters, and a dedicated 4-subwoofer management section with independent delay and phase alignment.

Spatial & Dynamics: Integrated Dolby Atmos, DTS:X, and Auro-3D surround panners alongside a custom dynamics section that models the unit's monolithic power stage.

Calibration Module: Native VST3 sidechain inputs and a dedicated calibration slot designed to run Dirac Live or Audyssey room-correction algorithms inside your DAW container

I have designed a comprehensive VST3 graphical user interface for the hypothetical Marantz Cinema 30 

DSP Channel Strip, capturing its complex internal architecture as a modular software rack.
The interface is structured into four main vertical sections, labeled across the top: Input & Preamp,  

Speaker Calibration & EQ, Surround Dynamics, and Output & Panner.
 
* Input & Preamp (HDAM SA-2): This module brings the hardware's signature analog warmth into your DAW. It features a large "HDAM SA-2 Drive" knob with a dedicated "Wound Toroidal" power status meter, input selection matrix, and high-pass filter.
 
* Speaker Calibration & EQ (Audyssey/Dirac): This section is dedicated to system tuning. It provides a parametric EQ visualization for simultaneous 13.4-channel control. Most notably, it includes a "Calibration Mode" slot with "Audyssey MultEQ XT32" selected and a dedicated "Add Dirac Live Slot" button for expandable room correction.
 
* Surround Dynamics (Monolithic Amp Model): This models the core power delivery. It provides 13.4-channel compressor/limiter controls with unique "Copper-Plate Shielding" and "Monolithic Amp" indicators.
 
* Output & Panner: The final section controls the spatial audio image. It features a sophisticated top-down surround panner with visual positioning for the full 13.4 layout and a dedicated module for independent management of the four subwoofers (delay, gain, and faders).
